{"availability":"available","full":"glampert/quake2-ps2","name":"quake2-ps2","description":"A homebrew port of idSoftware's Quake 2 for the PlayStation 2 Console.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":55,"forks":14,"created":"2015-10-26T19:36:26Z","updated":"2026-10-19T07:04:55Z","license":"GPL-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://glampert.github.io","topics":["game-development","homebrew-games","playstation2","ps2","ps2-homebrew","ps2dev","ps2sdk","quake2"],"demo":"https://glampert.github.io/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T13:44:39.935Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T13:44:39.935Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T13:44:39.935Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:23.277Z","stars":51,"forks":14},{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:20.678Z","stars":53,"forks":14},{"at":"2026-10-19T13:44:39.935Z","stars":55,"forks":14}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Tested on real hardware. The game boots and plays on a PS2, loading its data from a USB drive or PlayStation HDD, as well as in the PCSX2 emulator. Both TV standards are supported, PAL (50 Hz) and NTSC (60 Hz): auto-detected from the console, or forced with ps2videomode (also in the video options menu), so a PAL console can run at 60 Hz on a TV that takes it.","This is an unofficial fan-made port, targeting the PlayStation 2 console, of the original Quake II source code released by id Software.","The port relies solely on the free PS2DEV SDK to provide rendering, input, audio and system services for the Quake II engine — no official Sony SDK, no proprietary libraries. This project's goal is a fully functional and playable single-player Quake II on the PS2, built entirely with freely available tools."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/glampert/quake2-ps2/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"59d69a3428162ca7f55bd9979230f7fdc7f6204c528ed7aaf79ef45326d426ec","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:20.825Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:20